# notify.md — notification channel config

Used by `.forge/skills/request-human/notify.sh` to ping the human when an agent submits a `blocking` request. Non-blocking urgencies (`useful`, `nice-to-have`) log only.

Uncomment exactly one channel. Each is a shell command run with `$URGENCY`, `$REQUEST_ID`, and `$TITLE` available as env vars.

```sh
# --- Slack webhook ---
# curl -s -X POST -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
#   --data "{\"text\":\"[$URGENCY] $TITLE ($REQUEST_ID)\"}" \
#   "https://hooks.slack.com/services/T000/B000/secret-here"

# --- ntfy.sh ---
# curl -s -d "[$URGENCY] $TITLE ($REQUEST_ID)" \
#   "https://ntfy.sh/your-private-topic"

# --- email via sendmail ---
# printf 'Subject: [%s] wikiforge-{{domain}} request %s\n\n%s\n' \
#   "$URGENCY" "$REQUEST_ID" "$TITLE" \
#   | sendmail you@example.com

# --- log-only (default) ---
echo "[notify] $URGENCY | $REQUEST_ID | $TITLE" >> .forge/log.md
```
